Found the actual bug. Look at `todoist.ts:45-52`:

```js
if (!todoistTaskId) {
  const created = await todoistRequest("POST", `/api/v1/tasks`, body) as TodoistTask | null;
  if (created?.id) {
    todoistTaskId = created.id;
    await db.update(tasksTable).set({ todoistTaskId }).where(eq(tasksTable.id, task.id));
  }
  counters.created++;   // ← increments even when creation failed
}
```

`counters.created++` runs **unconditionally**, even when `created` comes back `null`. And `todoistRequest` returns `null` (instead of throwing) specifically on a `404` response:

```js
if (response.status === 404) return null;
```

So here's what's actually happening: your sync is hitting `POST /api/v1/tasks` for the "Show Tasks" workspace project and getting a **404 back from Todoist** — most likely because the OAuth-connected Todoist account doesn't have API-level create access to that Team Workspace project (workspace/shared-project permissions are a common gap for third-party integrations, separate from just being able to *see* the project in the picker via `GET /projects`). But the code swallows that 404, still counts it as "created," and shows you a success toast ("Pushed to Todoist: N created...") — while nothing was actually written to Todoist. That's exactly the symptom you're seeing.

Let me fix this so a failed create surfaces as an actual error instead of a false success:

